NODE id=matrix/neo/internal/writeback.Consolidator.ConsolidateSync kind=method
  digest=b3:c2380475380a502742653a63df2523b2b6098bfd25828f858f5f199e663ed152 file=neo/internal/writeback/consolidator.go range=115:140 lang=go exported=true byte_range=3551:5041
  sig=func (c *Consolidator) ConsolidateSync(ctx context.Context, transcript, conv string, seqLo, seqHi uint64)
  doc=ConsolidateSync runs the SAME extraction logic as Consolidate, but\nSYNCHRONOUSLY on the caller's goroutine — not through the async jobs\nchannel. It is called from compact() before evicting older turns so that\ndurable facts/events/patterns in the about-to-be-evicted transcript reach\ncortex BEFORE the turns are lost from the working window. This closes the\ngap where an async sweep could lag behind compaction and lose the last\nturns. The call respects the context deadline and never panics on a nil\nreceiver. It does NOT touch the async queue (steady-state is unchanged).
EDGES
  calls=matrix/neo/internal/writeback.Consolidator.allowed,matrix/neo/internal/writeback.Consolidator.process
  references=matrix/neo/internal/consolidation.Evidence,matrix/neo/internal/consolidation.EvidenceVerified,matrix/neo/internal/consolidation.Job,matrix/neo/internal/writeback.Consolidator,matrix/neo/internal/writeback.Consolidator.allowed,matrix/neo/internal/writeback.Consolidator.process,matrix/neo/internal/writeback.c,matrix/neo/internal/writeback.cancel,matrix/neo/internal/writeback.conv,matrix/neo/internal/writeback.ctx,matrix/neo/internal/writeback.seqHi,matrix/neo/internal/writeback.seqLo,matrix/neo/internal/writeback.subCtx,matrix/neo/internal/writeback.sum,matrix/neo/internal/writeback.transcript
  ^contains=matrix/neo/internal/writeback.Consolidator
  ^defines=matrix/neo/internal/writeback/consolidator.go

